8 Accounts
**********

‘M-x harmless-login’ signs in.  If several connections exist, it asks
which one.  ‘M-x harmless-logout’ forgets the Harmless token for that
connection.  It does not delete a token that belongs to Grok Build,
Claude Code, or Codex.

xAI
===

Browser login opens ‘auth.x.ai’.  Harmless listens on port 56121.
Tokens are stored under ‘harmless-directory’, mode 0600, and refresh on
their own.  A prefix argument uses the device-code flow.  Harmless also
uses that flow when port 56121 is already taken, for example by Grok
Build.

   If you have already run ‘grok login’ and ‘harmless-xai-use-grok-auth’
is non-nil, Harmless reuses ‘~/.grok/auth.json’ until you sign in or out
from Emacs.  It never writes that file.  A refresh is saved under
‘harmless-directory’ instead.

   An API key still works when no OAuth session is active.  Put it in
‘~/.authinfo’ as ‘machine api.x.ai login apikey password xai-...’, or
export ‘XAI_API_KEY’.

OpenAI
======

Login opens ChatGPT OAuth and listens on ‘localhost:1455’.  A prefix
argument asks you to paste the redirect URL. Harmless also does that
when port 1455 is busy.  Tokens go in ‘auth-openai.json’.  A still-valid
‘~/.codex/auth.json’ is reused and never written.

   ChatGPT subscription tokens are sent to the Codex Responses API, not
to ‘api.openai.com’.  ‘OPENAI_API_KEY’ remains a usage-based fallback on
Chat Completions.

Anthropic
=========

Login uses Claude Code's OAuth client.  The browser shows a code.  Paste
it at the minibuffer prompt.  Tokens go in ‘auth-anthropic.json’.  A
still-valid ‘~/.claude/.credentials.json’ access token is reused.
Harmless does not write or refresh that file.

Several accounts
================

Give each account its own connection name.  The default names keep the
original files: ‘auth.json’, ‘auth-openai.json’, and
‘auth-anthropic.json’.  Any other name gets ‘auth-SLUG.json’.  A session
stays on the connection it was given.  One buffer can use a personal
Grok account while another uses a work Claude account.

   A local server has no browser login.


