18 Trouble
**********

‘M-x harmless-abort’, or ‘a’ in the transcript, or ‘C-c C-a’ in the
prompt, cancels the HTTP request or the shell command that is running.
The session returns to idle and the transcript records ‘aborted’.

   An empty reply from the model is an error: ‘The model returned an
empty reply.’

   Diagnostic lines go to the buffer ‘*harmless-log*’.  The buffer keeps
at most ‘harmless-log-max-lines’ lines (2000).  Do not put an API key in
a note you expect to see there.  The log is not written to disk.

   ‘M-x harmless-reload-all-harmless’ loads every ‘.el’ file beside the
‘harmless.el’ Emacs actually loaded.  It skips ‘harmless-autoloads.el’
and prefers a newer source file over a byte-compiled copy.  Restart
Emacs when a live session was created before a session field was added.
Reloading does not rebuild this manual.  *Note Manual::.


File: harmless.info,  Node: Manual,  Next: Command Index,  Prev: Trouble,  Up: Top

19 Manual
*********

This book is an Info manual.  Open it with ‘M-x harmless-info’, with ‘h’
in a Harmless buffer, or with ‘h’ in the Harmless menu.  After Harmless
has loaded, ‘C-h i’ lists it in the Emacs directory.

   The source is ‘doc/harmless.texi’ next to ‘lisp’.  The file Emacs
reads is ‘doc/harmless.info’.  Rebuild it from the repository root:

     make manual

   That needs ‘makeinfo’, from the Texinfo package.  Commit both the
Texinfo source and the generated Info file.  A change to a command, a
key, a tool, or a permission belongs in the manual in the same change.


